Track 1: The Hawser Chews the Piling
- Story & Context: When a catastrophic tidal backsurge flooded Shaft Four at the Nicaro terminal, foreman Elier Cruz and his shift crew were pinned against the bulkhead in chest-high brine with the power grids completely dead. To keep hypothermia and hysteria from breaking the group, Cruz started hammering a frantic 3:2 clave against a hollow steel ventilation stack with his ratchet, prompting thirty miners to lock into a deafening percussive counter-rhythm that resonated all the way to the harbor cranes above. By the time emergency divers cut through the ceiling hatch, the deafening acoustic roar of metal on ductwork had evolved into a furious, collective scream of defiance: "Breathe through the iron before the harbor drowns the cage!"
