Track 2: Zero-Crossing at Dead Low Water
- Story & Context: Sound technician and clandestine smuggler Dayana Véliz tracked this agonizing confession inside the corroded engine casing of an abandoned suction dredge at low tide, running her microphone cable through an intake pipe to capture the hollow acoustic ring of the mudflats. Haunted by the crew of mechanics she accidentally locked behind a blast valve during a privateer raid on the fuel lines, she loops an aching, screaming electric violin line that mimics coastal distress beacons over a punishing, half-time baritone guitar crawl. The track strips the timba tempo down to a suffocating, drag-heavy groove as she whispers and then roars her confession into the damp: "I traded your lungs for thirty knots of clear water."
