Track 3: “Did You Sound the Fog-Bell?”
- Story & Context: Decades after the lower conduit network beneath Punta Gorda was sealed off with four thousand tons of industrial slag, local harbor tugboat operators still claim to hear syncopated clave taps vibrating up through the hulls during heavy sea mists. The myth centers on Osmany, a renegade violinist who vanished into the access shafts with a custom wireless amplifier and swore he would play until the salt choked his strings. To this day, young dock workers gather along the seawall during storm warnings, hammering crowbars against empty shipping containers to see if the drowned orchestra beneath the seabed answers back: "Ring it twice for the living, ring it hard for the deep!"
